      },
      "rev_n_3_eec0b0_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_eec0b0_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_eec0b0",
        "thought_text": "For each train, calculate the latest acceptable departure time to ensure the total journey time is at least 1800 seconds, then find the minimum of these times.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794408066.727412
      },
      "rev_n_4_84f462_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_84f462_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_84f462",
        "thought_text": "The current approach checks if a train can reach the destination within 30 minutes after accounting for delays. However, it does not consider the possibility of chaining multiple trains to reach the destination. We need to explore paths involving multiple trains and ensure the total travel time exceeds 30 minutes.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "834887023283777278",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794408137.789549
      },
      "rev_n_5_78206c_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_78206c_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_78206c",
        "thought_text": "Instead of sorting trains by departure time, consider sorting them by the difference between their planned arrival and departure times. This might help in identifying trains that have longer travel durations, which could be crucial for ensuring the total journey time exceeds 30 minutes.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "834887023283777278",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794408137.78957
      },
      "rev_n_6_6cfe0f_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_6cfe0f_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_6cfe0f",
        "thought_text": "Implement a breadth-first search (BFS) or depth-first search (DFS) algorithm to explore all possible train paths from station 1 to station N. For each path, calculate the total travel time considering delays and check if it exceeds 30 minutes. Track the earliest start time that meets this condition.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "834887023283777278",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794408137.789581
      },
      "rev_n_7_b593f5_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_7_b593f5_0",
        "node_id": "n_7_b593f5",
        "thought_text": "Re-evaluate the calculation of travel time. The travel time for each train should be the sum of the planned travel time and the delay, not the difference between the arrival and departure times.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-4212137488070906516",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794408172.856561
      },
      "rev_n_8_1a7b59_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_8_1a7b59_0",
        "node_id": "n_8_1a7b59",
        "thought_text": "Consider using a different algorithm, such as Bellman-Ford, to handle potential negative weights resulting from delays.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-4212137488070906516",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794408172.856587
      },
      "rev_n_9_864252_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_9_864252_0",
        "node_id": "n_9_864252",
        "thought_text": "Implement a check to ensure that the calculated total travel time for any path is at least 1800 seconds. If no such path exists, return 'impossible'.",
